## Key Scoring Tools

### FAST (Stroke)
- Face droop
- Arm weakness
- Speech disturbance
- Time of onset

### Sepsis Red Flags (Adult)
- Temperature > 38.3 or < 36
- HR > 90, RR > 20
- Altered mental status
- Suspected infection source
- Lactate > 2 mmol/L â†’ sepsis; > 4 â†’ septic shock

### AVPU / GCS
- Alert (GCS 15)
- Voice (GCS ~13)
- Pain (GCS ~8)
- Unresponsive (GCS < 8) â†’